A borderless pop-up (0002) is at the floating level. GPUI put every `WindowKind::PopUp` at `NSPopUpWindowLevel` (101),
so the quick terminal's panel was above the floating panels of other apps. Upstream agterm's `QuickTerminalPanel` sets
`level = .floating` (3). Now a pop-up without a title bar gets `NSFloatingWindowLevel`. Its collection behavior does
not change (all spaces, full-screen auxiliary), so it still shows on each space and over a full-screen app. A pop-up
with a title bar stays at `NSPopUpWindowLevel`. scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies this to the verified crates.io archive.

diff -ruN a/src/window.rs b/src/window.rs
--- a/src/window.rs
+++ b/src/window.rs
@@ -1236,7 +1236,12 @@
                 WindowKind::PopUp | WindowKind::AnchoredPopup(_) => {
                     add_mouse_tracking_area(tracking_view);
 
-                    native_window.setLevel_(NSPopUpWindowLevel);
+                    // A borderless panel floats over normal windows, not over other apps' floating panels.
+                    native_window.setLevel_(if borderless {
+                        NSFloatingWindowLevel
+                    } else {
+                        NSPopUpWindowLevel
+                    });
                     if borderless {
                         // A borderless window has no shadow until it asks for one.
                         let _: () = msg_send![native_window, setHasShadow: YES];
